<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Romans 8:26 says the Spirit &laquo;intercedes for us with groanings too deep for words.&raquo; Think of a time when you were in so much pain, confusion, or darkness that you could not pray — the words would not come, or you did not even want to pray. Looking back, can you see signs that Someone was holding you and praying in you? What does it change to know you were never praying alone?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">This question may touch something tender. That&apos;s okay. Write what is true, even if it is hard.</p>
