<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;The Spirit helps us in our weakness, for we do not know how to pray as we ought, but the Spirit himself intercedes for us with groanings too deep for words. And he who searches the hearts knows what is the mind of the Spirit, because the Spirit intercedes for the saints according to the will of God.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Romans 8:26-27</p>
</div>

<p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:8px"><strong>Tip for memorizing:</strong> Read it aloud three times. Then cover the text and try to say it from memory. Repeat once a day. By the end of the week, it will be yours.</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Come, Holy Spirit,<br />
fill the heart of your faithful<br />
and kindle in them the fire of your love.</p>
<p>Come, father of the poor,<br />
come, giver of gifts,<br />
come, light of hearts.</p>
<p>You are the best consoler,<br />
the soul&apos;s sweet guest,<br />
refreshment in the heat of the day.</p>
<p>In labor, you are rest;<br />
in the scorching sun, you are the shade;<br />
in tears, you are comfort.</p>
<p>O most blessed Light,<br />
fill the deepest places of my heart.<br />
Without your strength, nothing in us is strong,<br />
nothing is holy.</p>
<p>Wash what is unclean,<br />
water what is dry,<br />
heal what is wounded.</p>
<p>Bend what is rigid,<br />
warm what is cold,<br />
guide what has gone astray.</p>
<p>Give to your faithful<br />
who trust in you<br />
your seven holy gifts.</p>
<p>Give us the reward of virtue,<br />
give us the salvation that has no end,<br />
give us joy that lasts forever.<br />
Amen. Alleluia.</p>
<p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:12px">&mdash; Adapted from the &laquo;Veni Sancte Spiritus&raquo; Sequence</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

